From ce60df7149ef204efc77735f8b0d41d7cc6a8e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kevin.krausse" <kkrausse97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:19:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add intense-narration version of the continuous Gromen
 film

Re-voices the continuous Bondfire scene with Orpheus 3B (voice dan,
temperature 0.9) so the narrator builds from level to shouting. The
choreography is not copied: gromen-intense includes the continuous
scene's main.rs and runs it against its own narration timeline.

Orpheus has no emotion control, so the build comes from the written
form of each line (script.json 'say') plus shouted lead/tail sentences
that are generated around the later lines and then cut out. Block
times come from transcribing the takes, and the script's gapAfter
pauses are restored by padding silence at the cut points. It is six
takes joined in the silent gaps, not one continuous take.

The delivery step skips loudnorm so the rising level survives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
